{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1352224-martial-arts-compatibility","id":1352224,"title":"Martial Arts Compatibility","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-02T14:44:13-08:00","id":1352224,"title":"Martial Arts Compatibility","content":"Someone had a question on here about which Martial Arts are compatible with others based on Form Weapons or Complimentary Abilities. It sounded like a fun project so I threw a quick sheet together. No idea if something like this already exists, but a cursory search didn't turn anything up and I needed the thought experiment for my brain.<br /> <br /> Behold, the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1pTdB_WOdaR5osLns8QykO3mwi7c2KvQScecqyBuONXw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Martial Art Style Compatibility Sheet</a>. (You will have to Make a Copy to use it, I will not grant anyone Edit rights to the original)<br /> <br /> With this you can see all the compatible Armor types, Form Weapons, and Complimentary Abilities and sort by them. It's a bit of a bonkers bit of code so it's possible it'll miss something but I <b>think</b> I tested all the possible combinations. I went through the Core book, DB book, and Lunars book to get the styles but if anyone is aware of more content please let me know. It's actually pretty easy to fill in your own data on the Data tab. Just make sure to follow the format and the rest should just work!<br /> <br /> Let me know how it works!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T15:04:13-08:00","id":1352229,"title":"","content":"1. That's really cool and usefull!<br /> <br /> 2. It seems to be missing Laughing Monsters Style from Lunars (Unarmed, Staff, War Fan, Whip).<br /> <br /> 3. It lists styles using seven-section staffs and regular staff when choosing staff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","user":"limaxophobiac","date":". 12-02-2019, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2579-limaxophobiac","name":"limaxophobiac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"294"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T15:19:58-08:00","id":1352232,"title":"","content":"Tiger Style is listed as No Armor only, when it should allow for Light Armor as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","na